@startuml
title RuleSphere - Protect and Persist Execution Evidence\nUC-24
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #177E8D
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #EAF6F8

participant EvaluationService as Runtime
participant TraceCaptureService as Capture
participant SensitiveDataProtector as Protect
database "Hot Trace Store" as Hot
database "Compliance Ledger" as Ledger
participant "Operational Telemetry" as Ops

Runtime ->> Capture: Capture execution tree, snapshot metadata and outcome
activate Capture

Capture -> Protect: Protect sensitive fields using bound schema metadata
activate Protect
Protect --> Capture: Masked / tokenized / hashed evidence
deactivate Protect

note over Capture,Protect
  Protect intermediate values, final outcomes and error details
  before persistence. No plaintext sensitive trace fields (SRS 11.1).
end note

par Full trace persistence
  Capture -> Hot: Persist protected execution tree
  activate Hot
  Hot --> Capture: Persistence result
  deactivate Hot
else Long-term metadata persistence
  Capture -> Ledger: Persist immutable ExecutionID, DecisionVersion, InputHash,\nprotected Output, MatchedNodeIDs, Timestamp, approval/release reference
  activate Ledger
  Ledger --> Capture: Persistence result
  deactivate Ledger
end

alt Both writes succeed
  Capture -> Ops: Record capture success
  activate Ops
  Ops --> Capture: Acknowledged
  deactivate Ops
else Persistence failure or backpressure
  Capture -> Ops: Report affected execution, failure and degradation
  activate Ops
  Ops --> Capture: Acknowledged
  deactivate Ops
  Capture -> Capture: Apply operational failure / backpressure policy
  note over Runtime,Capture
    Never silently change the business decision outcome.
    Delivery guarantees, retries and failure policy require ADR;
    asynchronous arrows do not prescribe a broker or queue.
  end note
end
deactivate Capture

note over Hot,Ledger
  Hot trace retention: configured 30-90 days.
  Compliance metadata retention: configured 5-7 years (SRS 11).
end note
@enduml
